the son of a female slave; (the proper employment of
a Kṣattṛ is said to be catching animals that live in
holes); a N. of Vidura as the son of a female slave,
his father being the celebrated Vyāsa (see Mahā-bh.
1. 7381); an epithet of Brahmā; a fish.

क्षप् 2. क्षप्, cl. 10. P. क्षपयति, -यि-
तुम्, to send, throw, cast, direct, &c.;
[cf. Goth. skapa.]

क्षम्प् क्षम्प्, cl. 1. or 10. P. क्षम्पति
or क्षम्पयति, -यितुम्, to suffer, bear;
[cf. 1. क्षम्.]

1. क्षयण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. habitable (?); (अस्),
m. a place with tranquil water; a bay, harbour (?);
(अम्), n. a dwelling-place.

क्षयिन्, ई, इणी, इ, wasting, decaying, fragile;
consumptive.
—क्षयि-त्व, अम्, n. fragility.
